<section id="en-control"><span aria-hidden="true" class="wiki-anchor-alias" id="Fortress_Control"></span><h2>AIMy / Tinker: four shared control tracks</h2><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Track</th><th scope="col">Level 1 → 10</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Fortress Resilience</th><td data-label="Level 1 → 10">12 → 30</td><td data-label="Effect">+2 starting Lives per level; does not restore Lives already lost.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Barrier Deployment</th><td data-label="Level 1 → 10">6 → 24</td><td data-label="Effect">+2 whole-battle base uses per ordinary barrier design, per level.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Structural Reinforcement</th><td data-label="Level 1 → 10">100% → 235%</td><td data-label="Effect">+15 percentage points to purchased-barrier HP multiplier per level; no turret or hero HP.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Turret Control</th><td data-label="Level 1 → 10">3 → 12</td><td data-label="Effect">+1 to the shared active-turret cap per level.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The shared cap is additional to design limits: Steamshot, Rotary Cannon and Rivet Driver allow three each, and every other turret two. Free shared capacity does not remove a design’s limit.</p><details><summary>Complete costs for all four control tracks</summary><details><summary>Fortress Resilience</summary><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Target level</th><th scope="col">Alloy</th><th scope="col">Circuitry</th><th scope="col">Reagents</th><th scope="col">Flux</th><th scope="col">Pristine Cores</th><th scope="col">Army EXP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td data-label="Alloy">36</td><td data-label="Circuitry">27</td><td data-label="Reagents">18</td><td data-label="Flux">9</td><td data-label="Pristine Cores">0</td><td data-label="Army EXP">225</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td data-label="Alloy">60</td><td data-label="Circuitry">45</td><td data-label="Reagents">30</td><td data-label="Flux">15</td><td data-label="Pristi